INSERT INTO `players_characters` VALUES ('02NQP3eNlI1Dikp','128','US','WhiteHead_17','76561198134507783','accepted',NULL,'active','Casey Jaice','12/18/1984','male','American','United Kingdom','Jaice comes from a background of law enforcement, having served his time in the Coast Guard and Sheriffs Department, he is looking for new opportunities, shall he re-join and do what he does best enforcing law, shall he open a business and see where that leads him, or shall he attempt to run a criminal empire.','2025-11-10 11:22:42','2025-11-10 21:02:57'),('07vWLllslcwgoEL','65','US','AfricanHead_01','76561198108019488','accepted',NULL,'inactive','Elijah Holmes','06/10/2002','male','American','United States','My name is Elijah Holmes, and I was born in Vespucci Beach, Los Santos, New York. I grew up in an affluent area in Los Santos, where my mother worked as a manager at the Los Santos bank. My father worked as an engineer on an oil rig. Growing up, my father would be gone for a couple of months at a time, working on the rig, so it was just my mom raising me. When he was home, I would ask him about his life working on the oil rig. He said that working on an oil rig was like being in a constant state of fear because anything could happen. He told me a story about one of his employees who was involved in a fire that broke out. He also told me that one day, I could be an engineer too. But deep down, I wanted nothing to do with oil rigs. The location was awful, being miles away from food, living with several other people in a confined space, and seeing the same waves crashing against the rig over and over. It would drive me crazy.','2025-11-05 17:26:14','2025-11-05 17:29:16'),('2diVcLXrtyPJUuL','113','US','WhiteHead_16','76561198120453492','accepted',NULL,'active','Alec Sickler','04/16/2002','male','American','United States','David told me to apply.','2025-11-05 16:48:15','2025-11-11 15:04:00'),('4ErOvzxKUIqfYCk','166','US','WhiteHead_24','76561198319377968','pending',NULL,'inactive','Lewis Williams','05/07/2003','male','British','United Kingdom','Lewis Williams lived his life in Wales, United Kingdom until he had enough with the way the country was being ran. He then began his process of applying for citizenship in the USA. Lewis had his goals on moving to Fisher’s Island, New York. He always heard about the American dream and wanted to be apart of it. Lewis strives on being a lawful citizen and hopes to join the FISD one day, and work his way up the ranks to prove to everyone that an emigrated citizen is capable of achieving the best.','2025-11-11 20:15:06','2025-11-11 21:07:16'),('5fsEq7Rtz2oXFn7','144','US','WhiteHead_27','76561199063624238','accepted',NULL,'inactive','Kyle Foster','01/18/2001','male','Scottish','Scotland, UK','Kyle Foster was born in Inverness, Scotland, in 2001, the youngest of three children in a working-class family. His father, Alistair Foster, worked long shifts as a mechanic, while his mother, Moira, ran a small bakery known for her oatcakes and shortbread. Growing up near the River Ness, Kyle developed a love for the outdoors — hiking through the Highlands, fishing with his dad, and helping tourists find their way when they got lost in the misty glens.','2025-11-02 22:56:45','2025-11-10 09:58:48'),('5tyhhotVZVHcaNB','58','US','WhiteHead_06','76561198220382296','accepted',NULL,'active','Kaelen Cerberus','06/15/2001','male','Australian','Australia','I moved from the eastern coast of Australia, where I used to work as a reserved military pilot for the ADF (Australian Defence force) and since moving to the area, wanted to get back into flying but with another purpose. My goal is to be able to join FIFR and try to become a S.A.R. Pilot using my skills to help people that need it and learn how to do it right.','2025-11-02 22:13:09','2025-11-11 05:50:47'),('8AAVDQpNCkYkcKy','55','US','WhiteHead_20','76561198347114693','pending',NULL,'inactive','Alex Blackwater','11/24/1999','male','British','United Kingdom','Alex Blackwater wasn’t the kind of bloke you’d mistake for a saint. Born and raised in the industrial outskirts of London, he learned early on that the world didn’t hand you anything—you had to take it. His father, a steelworker turned drunk, left when Alex was ten. His mother worked double shifts at a textile plant to keep food on the table, leaving Alex to raise himself most days. By sixteen, he was already running with older lads, doing “favours” for cash—moving packages, keeping watch, and, when needed, using his fists.\r\n\r\nAlex was clever, though. Smarter than most of the people he ran with. While the rest were brawling for scraps, he was learning how the world really worked—who paid who, how to move quietly, and how to make something disappear without anyone asking questions. It wasn’t long before he became known in the Midlands underground as a man who could sort things out. Whether that meant fixing a problem or making one vanish, Alex got it done.\r\n\r\nBut intelligence doesn’t erase consequences. His work eventually caught the attention of the wrong kind of people—those who didn’t take kindly to freelancing. After a job in Manchester went south, involving a shipment that was meant to “fall off the lorry,” Alex found himself hunted by both the law and his former associates. One night, his flat was raided. He slipped out through the back, left everything behind, and disappeared.\r\n\r\nFor months, Alex drifted between safe houses, moving up and down the coast under different names. During those quiet, sleepless nights, something in him began to shift. He was tired—tired of running, tired of watching his back, tired of wondering if the next knock at the door would be his last. He’d spent his life surviving, not living.\r\n\r\nWhen he first heard about Fisher’s Island, it sounded almost unreal—a quiet place across the Atlantic, far from the chaos of the UK underworld. A community small enough for a man to disappear, but civil enough for him to rebuild. He scraped together what little he had left, bought a one-way ticket under a new identity, and left England behind.\r\n\r\nArriving on Fisher’s Island, Alex tried to keep his head down. The accent gave him away immediately, but people seemed to like it—or at least, tolerate it. He found work where he could: fixing engines, helping at the docks, running supplies between towns. He wasn’t above getting his hands dirty, but this time, he wanted to earn an honest living.\r\n\r\nStill, the past doesn’t let go easily. There are nights when he sits by the harbour, cigarette glowing in the dark, thinking about the things he’s done—the people he’s hurt, the deals gone bad. He tells himself he’s different now, that this island is a fresh start. But deep down, Alex knows it’s a fine line he’s walking. He’s a man with rough edges, sharp instincts, and a history that could burn it all down if he lets it.\r\n\r\nFor now, though, Alex Blackwater is just another face on Fisher’s Island. A man trying to go straight, to build something real from the wreckage of his past. Whether he succeeds or not—that’s a story still being written.','2025-11-11 19:51:46','2025-11-11 19:51:47'),('a45IgVjn3Jxdy8r','1','US','WhiteHead_06','76561198170351694','accepted',NULL,'active','Franklin Hawks','10/20/2000','male','American','USA','sqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqq','2025-11-08 15:56:55','2025-11-10 12:27:36'),('BKtLZ2t12dZtU7B','29','US','Kerry','76561198297605366','accepted',NULL,'active','Victor Sorrento','05/06/2008','male','American','United States','Victor Sorrento is on his last leg, having struggled through a series of failed jobs and unsuccessful business ventures. Each setback has weighed heavily on him, but he refuses to give up. Hoping for a fresh start, he plans to move to Fishers Island to rebuild his life from the ground up. His greatest motivation is his desire to become a dependable provider for his family back home. Despite the challenges, Victor remains determined, with a steady job already lined up that offers honest, meaningful work.','2025-11-06 04:50:24','2025-11-10 06:27:55'),('c0q2uhoIB9ssUsE','134','US','Miller','76561198080532671','accepted',NULL,'active','Tom Archer','03/25/1998','male','British, American','United Kingdom','Born to One British and one American Parent, I was born with the rare opportunity of dual citizenship, I have lived in both countries at varying points in my life as my father was in the American Military Stationed at RAF Lakenheath (USAF 48th Fighter Wing) as a Aviation Firefighter, My mother was British, they met in london, I have lived in varying places around the world since then.\r\n\r\nNow I am deciding to emigrate to Fishers Island, as a contributing member of society, have recently given the opportunity to become a Lieutenant within Fisher Island Fire Rescue and I plan to contribute and succeed in my role to the island as a whole.\r\n\r\nps.\r\n\"David told me to apply\"','2025-10-29 18:13:38','2025-11-11 16:45:06'),('C9xTVuvLC74b4Kk','94','US','WhiteHead_08','76561198251495864','accepted',NULL,'active','Jeff Haas','07/19/1999','male','American','United States','DAVID MESSED UP THE APPS.','2025-10-30 00:50:20','2025-11-11 19:41:57'),('D9D7iUsjVC1Sx8V','50','US','MaleHead_02','76561198277224587','accepted',NULL,'active','Markus Smidy','05/22/2003','male','Canadian','CA','Markus Is 22 years old And  He was born and raised In Utah He was a Farmer Living in Utah with His  parents He grew up On a farm And started doing jobs around the farm when He was only 8 years old After Finishing up collage He started  up His own Fast Food Place It was going all so well until one day The people who Normally came in Stopped coming in anymore  after a while He had to let go his employees cause he couldn\'t afford to pay his employees the next day his business went  under and he was forced to shutdown his fast food place years later he got enough money to move into a house/apartment  in  APL Markus Is a kind boy who never gave up  on friends he even helped out a grandma carry her begs and helped her to her car, he also was loved by everyone in his town he is very sweet boy  and he would never hurt anyone unless  they hurt him or his love ones.','2025-10-30 14:53:49','2025-11-11 04:55:30'),('DchR0CbYumVSDBd','153','US','WhiteHead_20','76561198164834098','accepted',NULL,'active','Reece Foster','06/24/1994','male','British','United Kingdom','Reece Foster. A 30 year old man who\'s up-bringing was rough as his parents separated at the age of 4 and his father moved up north to start a new life with a new woman and thankfully his mother finding another man to fill the void. His education consists of not a great upbringing with education due to his behaviour through secondary school. Thankfully as he progressed into college, his maturity grew and found himself in college undertaking Mechanics, learning about cars and the parts it took to run a vehicle. As Reece grew from college, he found himself getting into a great point in life, getting his own property, own car however Unfortunately a year later, Reece Foster was nearly made homeless due to his constant spending of money and is loss of control with his money, this landed Reece in serious problems with overcoming his issues. Thankfully after sitting down with professional help, Reece Foster was able to overcome these issues and get himself back onto a correct way of life with his money problem. Reece has always had the passion to follow his dream to become a Police Officer and climb the ranks to help lead a successful service. Law Enforcement has always been a special place in his heart as he has had family members in the emergency services and has been a big role model for Reece Foster of which Reece Foster hopes to be able to follow his passion and role model in the up-bringing of the Police Service. Once Reece has found his feet within the city, made some friends and got to know more of the details with the police service he will apply, What Reece loves about everyday in this kind of job is not everyday is the same meaning there\'s room for surprises.','2025-11-05 20:16:31','2025-11-05 22:33:35'),('EspKarmEFcd6QGI','152','US','WhiteHead_27','76561198447260307','accepted',NULL,'inactive','Jordan Belfort','09/30/2000','male','British','UK','Jordan Belfort is a man driven by ambition, charisma, and a hunger for success that never quite fades. Once the mastermind behind a booming empire that crashed as fast as it rose, his name still echoes in business circles — both admired and feared. After years of reflection and rebuilding, Jordan’s set his sights on the island, ready to launch a new venture and prove he’s more than his past mistakes. He’s older, wiser, but no less relentless. Every move is calculated, every deal a step toward redemption. Some say he’s changed, others say a wolf never loses its bite — either way, Jordan Belfort is back, and he’s ready to take the island by storm.','2025-11-05 10:01:45','2025-11-05 10:01:45'),('GGRdtXdmPS8rmff','164','US','WhiteHead_03','76561198172900082','accepted',NULL,'active','Tony Dapone','05/22/1990','male','American','United States','Tony Dapone, born on the fifth of May, 1990, to a blue collar family in Brooklyn, always knew he would be a millionaire. He had been working at it all his life.  From the young age of 12, he had been hustling anyway he could to make some cash. Cleaning cars, selling on the streets, if it could get him one step closer he\'d do it. Once he had his drivers license, he began driving trucks for his uncle off the books. Overtime, he learned the ins and outs of trucking in the city, and ending up buying a used tow truck. Slowly growing his company, Tony climbed the ranks in the citys towing game. Greed got the most of him, and he ended up getting caught up with an illegal car boosting ring. With a two year prison sentence, and enough money to buy a truck he has no choice but do the time and pack of shop and start over somewhere new.','2025-11-10 02:31:37','2025-11-11 14:24:56'),('Gn5hSt3GWw4iwBk','157','US','mgsr_snakeface','76561198343650521','accepted',NULL,'active','Nikitas Stoned','04/17/1997','male','Greek','Russia','They call me Nikitas — Stoned, because I learned early that the world only respects what it can’t bend. Born in a cramped Fisher’s Island trailer, I grew up to the brine of the harbor and the clatter of docks. My father taught me how to gut a fish; the streets taught me how to gut a man’s reputation. By sixteen I was in and out of county lockups, a kid with too much anger and not enough options. The island’s smallness sharpened everyone’s edges; rival crews, crooked dealers, bored cops — a pressure cooker of tired men and bad choices.\r\n\r\nI built a name the hard way: loyalty traded like currency, survival traded like breath. I sold what people wanted, took what was owed, and when the law came knocking I learned to disappear. But the noise followed — the headlines, the losses, the nights when I woke up to someone else’s child’s cry. Killing cops is the kind of thing that either makes you a ghost or buries you under a thousand eyes. I’ve stared at both outcomes.\r\n\r\nMotivation isn’t just money or fear; it’s the itch to prove I’m not the island’s forgotten son. I want respect — not from paper, but from the people who matter, from the ones who remember where I came from. My goals are messy: protect my crew, carve out a slice of safety for the ones who stayed, and one day walk off the docks knowing my name won’t drag someone else down.\r\n\r\nBut every hard choice costs. The ledger of my life is full of names and faces I didn’t mean to take. Lately I feel the pull to change the balance: keep the street smarts, lose the needless violence, and maybe, just maybe, trade the finality of revenge for something that lasts longer than a headline. If I can find a way off the island that doesn’t cost another life, I’ll take it. Until then, I move like tidewater — patient, inevitable, and with a weight that no small town can wash away.','2025-11-06 01:18:55','2025-11-10 23:13:54'),('jIdTHp87dG2AAME','7','US','WhiteHead_16','76561198147147468','accepted',NULL,'active','Matthew Evans','11/12/1989','male','American','United States','David told me to apply.','2025-11-05 16:48:15','2025-11-09 03:04:20'),('LFRqUj57dQLf7LW','46','US','AfricanHead_01','76561198193245617','accepted',NULL,'active','King Tyrone','10/07/1997','male','American, Portuguese, British','Guernsey','My name is Tyrone King, and I come from a small, rough patch of land called Red Water County. If you’ve ever been there, you’d know it’s not the kind of place that makes life easy. The streets are cracked, the lights flicker at night, and most folks either keep their heads down or fall into trouble. Growing up there, trouble had a way of finding you whether you wanted it or not, and for a long time, I didn’t do much to avoid it.\r\n\r\nAs a kid, I didn’t have much. My mom worked two jobs just to keep the lights on, and my dad was never around. The older guys in the neighborhood became my role models. They had nice cars, fancy clothes, and respect. I thought that was the way out, the only way. Before I knew it, I was running with a local crew, doing small jobs at first, then bigger ones. We told ourselves it was just business, just survival, but deep down I knew it wasn’t the kind of life that ended well.\r\n\r\nRed Water County had a way of swallowing people whole. You’d see friends disappear overnight, some to prison, some to the grave. I started losing people close to me—guys I grew up with, people I considered family. I began asking myself if that was really what I wanted. The more I thought about it, the more I realized I was just following a path that was laid out for me, not one I chose for myself.\r\n\r\nThe turning point came one night when everything went wrong. A deal turned into a shootout, and I barely made it out alive. I remember standing there afterward, breathing heavy, looking at what was left, and thinking, This can’t be it. This can’t be my life. That night, I made a promise to myself—I was done. I wanted something different. I wanted to build a life where I didn’t have to look over my shoulder all the time.\r\n\r\nSo, I left Red Water County behind. Packed up what little I had and started fresh. It wasn’t easy, starting over never is. But I’m determined to earn an honest living, to find real meaning in what I do. I’ve been looking for work, trying to keep my head down, learning to live right. I’m not perfect, and I don’t expect the world to hand me anything, but I’m ready to put in the work to make something of myself.\r\n\r\nI know my past will always be a part of me. Red Water County made me who I am, tough, loyal, and hungry for change. But it doesn’t define who I’m going to be. I’m Tyrone King, and I’m not running from my past anymore. I’m building my future, one step at a time.','2025-11-02 20:15:11','2025-11-02 20:38:08'),('lG7J3AWPT3ZM0VV','130','US','default','76561198868709203','accepted',NULL,'inactive','Olivia Foster','01/06/2001','female','white british','United Kingdom','Olivia Foster is a friendly, caring, and dedicated person who loves helping others and making new friends. Always smiling and approachable, she enjoys working with people and supporting her community. Olivia believes teamwork and kindness make every job easier. She’s known for her positive attitude, calm nature, and willingness to help anyone in need. Whether at work or around town, Olivia always puts others first and spreads positivity wherever she goes.','2025-11-02 23:08:41','2025-11-07 22:26:07'),('LiHha2Yx5ipz8dA','126','US','WhiteHead_17','76561198010461115','accepted',NULL,'active','Shawn Lorenzo','09/12/1991','male','American','United States','David told me to apply.\r\n\r\nAlready applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database. Already applied on old website database.','2025-10-30 03:03:45','2025-11-11 04:15:00'),('lZbGiqWnzwVaSjI','66','US','WhiteHead_16','76561198343727655','accepted',NULL,'active','Jamie Gargrave','06/09/2002','male','British','United Kingdom','I was birthed from a women into this world and here I am, just awesome. I am just some pretty cool dude if you ask me personally. However, I aspire to watch paint dry, that really entertains me and in my free time I like to bully random ants that I find. I want to find some ants and make friends with them here on Fishers. I am a pretty good friend.','2025-10-31 01:04:47','2025-11-09 18:43:39'),('m7LERyRbj3jP7mP','87','US','WhiteHead_17','76561198142911141','accepted',NULL,'active','Shane Foster','07/15/1997','male','Britsh','London, UK','hey im shane Foster The Owner Of Fosters Inc','2025-10-29 20:28:24','2025-11-11 15:22:25'),('OSeI5kmDhQxBSH1','19','US','WhiteHead_06','76561198111276670','accepted',NULL,'inactive','Erik Stanford','04/19/2000','male','American','United States','David told me to apply','2025-10-30 01:03:54','2025-10-30 01:03:55'),('pLw5EPCVeci99BU','104','US','WhiteHead_09','76561198039488098','accepted',NULL,'active','David Woods','12/15/2001','male','British','United Kingdom','I am the director, david told me to applyI am the director, david told me to applyI am the director, david told me to applyI am the director, david told me to applyI am the director, david told me to applyI am the director, david told me to applyI am the director, david told me to applyI am the director, david told me to applyI am the director, david told me to applyI am the director, david told me to applyI am the director, david told me to applyI am the director, david told me to applyI am the director, david told me to applyI am the director, david told me to applyI am the director, david told me to applyI am the director, david told me to applyI am the director, david told me to applyI am the director, david told me to applyI am the director, david told me to applyI am the director, david told me to applyI am the director, david told me to applyI am the director, david told me to apply','2025-10-30 08:21:33','2025-11-11 08:58:50'),('qwaLI8BKrczeq5D','110','US','WhiteHead_12','76561198125722747','accepted',NULL,'active','Nick Raven','02/12/2002','male','American','United States','Nick Raven is an entrepreneur who comes to Fishers Island wanting to grow and succeed. They came up from a working class family and will do whatever it takes to build themselves up to be successful, and he wants to own his own company on the island and run a business. Growing up as a working person and always doing whatever it takes to improve, he is ambitious, brave, and curious. A new start on fishers island with endless opportunity is something he looks forward to beginning on and growing to a prominent figure in the community is his dream.','2025-10-30 02:47:30','2025-11-10 22:24:21'),('RV0snIBPtLOGVXy','63','US','MaleHead_03','76561198133966379','accepted',NULL,'active','Jordan Hammer','07/18/2001','male','American','United States','Jordan Hammer is from Lakeside and has recently moved to this island. Mr. Hammer is a hard-working individual motivated to work and help the community. As a miner, I love to help out local businesses. Before moving here, I was a cop in Lakeside for a short time, obtaining the rank of Deputy. After retiring from law enforcement, I began mining and selling materials to local companies, such as those in the automotive industry. I also was a volunteer EMT for awhile to also give back to the community who held me so much.','2025-10-29 18:25:31','2025-11-11 03:40:44'),('upC0GQMPvutPQhy','114','US','WhiteHead_11','76561198001843859','accepted',NULL,'active','Malcolm Fairlie','06/10/1992','male','American','United States','Malcolm Fairley is a man that has a deep desire, of ambition, and a strong love for his family. He comes from a less fortunate family. He was being raised by both parents. Until he lost his mother or father due to a horrific car accident that took their lives, after the accident the only family he had left was his siblings. After years of abuse from multiple foster families once he turned 18 he decided that he would join the Marines so he could escape. This was not an easy choice for Malcolm because it meant leaving his siblings behind. Once he joined the Marines Time seemed to fly by. After 3 years Malcolm decided to pursue becoming a Marine Raider. After a little of a year passed he achieved his goal of becoming a Marine Raider. At this point he has become a part of one of the United States elite branches of military. After several years as a Marine Raider a mission went sideways far behind enemy lines where a couple of his comrades lost their lives.The loss of his comrade sent him into an unstable out of control rage. Although Malcolm doesn\'t quite recollect what happened the surviving comrades reported if it wasn’t for Malcolm\'s reckless behavior they might have not survived the mission, they never would have thought a man could have done what he had accomplished. After the mission ended Malcolm fell into deep depression. It seemed every time he would fall asleep he would relive the horrific sense of the mission. Once his term had ended he decided at this point in his life, that he no longer wanted to be a part of taking countless lives, he wanted to bring knowledge and joy to the world. Malcolm has worked hard his entire life to become the man he is today. Malcolm has never settled down to start a family due to being so ambitious. Now that he is out of the Marines, he looks forward to reconnecting with his siblings but fears that they might reject him for leaving. Once finding a place to settle down. He hopes to find a career that would \r\nHelp him achieve his goal of running a business and to gain great wealth so he is able to take care of his family and people in need. He\'s a fast learner and likes to help the less fortunate with hope of making new life long friends. He’s always liked the thought of giving a helping hand to his community. In the hopes of creating a place he never got to experience when he was going up. But this does not mean Malcolm is going to lay down and be walked over. If push came to shove and left no other option he will be forced into reverting back into the person he was to take care of business. Malcolm hopes that he’ll never be pushed into making such decisions. But he will not just set back and watch his goals turn into distance dreams.','2025-11-01 18:24:02','2025-11-11 04:31:27'),('VcWoB7iZt4IO7z0','100','US','WhiteHead_09','76561198170439869','accepted',NULL,'active','Chris OConnor','05/01/2002','male','American','United States','Chris OConnor is a quiet, practical operator from a coastal town with an indistinct past; he shows up where things break and prefers doing the work over explaining why. He stabilizes injured people and unstable situations, runs small, adaptable teams, and keeps certain documents and debts guarded like tools in a kit. Few know what truly drives him—part curiosity, part obligation—but he carries a private plan to someday earn a pilot’s license, a loose promise that reads like escape and discipline at once. His aims are intentionally vague: protect those nearby, answer lingering questions about old mistakes, and build a handful of trusted allies who move when he signals.','2025-10-29 18:14:26','2025-10-31 03:02:48'),('VeGSFwD7n7K5ORd','101','US','WhiteHead_11','76561199531609151','accepted',NULL,'active','Jack Branson','05/26/2003','male','American','United States','Jack Branson grew up believing money makes the world go ’round. Raised in a family-run construction business, he learned hard work, the art of negotiation, and how to turn contracts into profit. When Jack arrived on the island he started fresh as a legitimate entrepreneur — selling tools, running a food stand, and supplying fuel — but honest work only got him so far. Practical and pragmatic, he began to apply his deal-making skills to the street economy.\r\n\r\nTo Jack, crime is just another business model: risk, margins, and reputation matter more than violence. He isn’t a thrill-seeking outlaw — he’s careful, disciplined, and focused on building a secure future. His motivation is simple: freedom and stability. He wants enough money to expand his legal enterprises, buy property, and provide for those he cares about. His goal is to climb out of uncertainty without becoming the kind of brute the sheriffs write about; he prefers quiet, profitable schemes that fly under the radar. Smart, likable, and morally flexible, Jack walks the line between respectability and the shadow economy — always negotiating his next move.','2025-11-09 16:46:22','2025-11-09 23:20:49'),('VGTAbf0x5NCQSJv','151','US','WhiteHead_17','76561198279616292','accepted',NULL,'active','Joshua Blackwater','04/22/1999','male','British','United Kingdom','Joshua Blackwater is a name that carries weight across the island — a man as charming as he is ruthless. Known for his sharp suits, sharper deals, and the mysterious “Blackwater Family” legacy, Joshua carved his reputation through calculated risks and bold moves that blurred the line between business and crime. Once involved in less-than-legal ventures, he’s since cleaned up his act… or so he claims. Now, Joshua’s determined to rebuild his empire from the ground up, pouring his ambition and cunning into legitimate enterprise. But whispers of his past never quite fade. People still wonder whether he’s truly changed or just found smarter ways to make his fortune. Either way, Joshua Blackwater is back — and he’s ready to make the island his again.','2025-11-05 09:44:49','2025-11-10 21:20:38'),('vnGrGTQIjRCrBZv','132','US','RussianHead_5','76561198318844013','accepted',NULL,'inactive','Alex Anderson','05/22/1999','male','American','United States','Alex Anderson is the most prestigious legal mind lurking among the many creatures of Fisher\'s Island','2025-11-11 05:31:59','2025-11-11 05:32:00'),('WryScKSN9gOyCZT','156','US','GreekHead_A3_05','76561198030730338','accepted',NULL,'inactive','Austin Farley','03/19/1996','male','American','United States','Austin Farley was born and raised in the rolling hills of Tennessee, where small-town values and hard work shaped who he became. From a young age, he was drawn to structure, purpose, and the idea of serving something bigger than himself. Right after finishing high school, Austin enlisted in the U.S. Army, eager to make a difference and see more of the world than his hometown offered. Over the years, he served with dedication and pride, gaining experience in logistics, leadership, and field operations. His time in the service taught him discipline, resilience, and how to stay calm when things got tough.\r\n\r\nAfter completing his service, Austin found the transition to civilian life harder than expected. The pace was slower, and the sense of direction he had in the Army was missing. Wanting to start fresh, he packed up and moved to the island of Altis, hoping to rebuild his life and find a new purpose. Whether it’s working as a mechanic, joining the local police or EMS, or running his own small business, Austin is focused on contributing to his community and building a stable future.\r\n\r\nAustin’s motivation comes from his desire to continue serving others — not through war, but through everyday acts of dedication and responsibility. He carries with him the lessons of his military career and the grounded values of his Tennessee upbringing, determined to make a positive impact wherever he goes.','2025-11-06 00:10:09','2025-11-11 03:14:53'),('XDLPFkgzIOC3RFx','15','US','WhiteHead_19','76561198030418313','accepted',NULL,'active','Chris Sutherland','12/16/1995','male','American','United States','David told me to apply','2025-10-29 20:48:24','2025-11-05 21:56:07'),('z4cUfsex8GnrU6Z','146','US','GreekHead_A3_04','76561198070895974','accepted',NULL,'active','Dick Axel','04/11/1955','male','American','US','Old man trying to make a new name for himself after losing everything. In his golden years, Dick was the most well respected auto mechanic in New York. At times his dementia kicks in reducing his ability to recall situations and memories, but he does try his absolute best. His goal is to find a new wife, and own the largest vehicle dealership in the city.','2025-11-03 05:31:45','2025-11-11 01:49:52'),('Za37XJbJhTqVnq9','136','US','WhiteHead_17','76561198109583767','accepted',NULL,'active','Ben Benson','10/02/2001','male','Irish','Ireland','Ben Benson is an Irish man who was born in Dublin, Ireland. He was raised by his mother and father in a middle class family who were just making it by week to week. Ben parents were good people who never got on the wrong side of the law however Ben surrounded himself with the wrong people and started to get involved with crime. It started off small with petty crimes but as he and his friends grew older they started getting involved with the drugs trade. At the start it was only small deals here and there but overtime they grew to one of the biggest and most influential gangs in the Kilkenny region. It all came crashing down when they were busted by the police when Ben was 18 years old. He got away quite lucky with only 5 years in prison and was released shortly after he turned 23. His family did not like the person he had become however and would not let him back into the house or the family. He lived on the streets for a few months before getting a job to save up for an apartment. Now he is looking to move to fishers island and start life again on the good side of the law by helping others wherever he can. Ben has no real goal of what he wants to do apart from help as many people as possible and see where this journey takes him','2025-10-30 18:42:02','2025-11-11 18:00:14'),('zH3ChEtToHzdOpl','140','US','LivonianHead_7','76561198075216298','accepted',NULL,'active','Josh Renot','06/20/1990','male','American','United States','I am a poor unskilled man, looking for the easiest ways to make money and survive on the island. My only goals are to get a decent vehicle, find a decent job to provide for my family, and buy a decent home. I do not want to be a criminal, but I am willing to turn a blind eye to the law, as long as it does not involve going against my morals.','2025-10-30 22:47:12','2025-11-10 23:34:59');
